## Question 5:  what is the sampling frame?

The PDHS 2017-18 used the complete list of enumeration blocks from the 2017 census as its frame, with a stratified two-stage design. 
In the first stage, 580 clusters were selected (561 surveyed), and in the second stage 28 households per cluster were sampled systematically. 
This means the survey covers children in households within census blocks, not a list of children. 
Because households and clusters had unequal selection probabilities, survey weights (v005) are needed for any population-level estimate. 
